## Part 7: VPN and Direct Connect

### VPN (Virtual Private Network)

A **VPN** creates a secure, encrypted connection between your on-premises network and your VPC.

#### VPN Architecture:

```
On-Premises Data Center          AWS Cloud
┌──────────────────────────────┐ ┌─────────────────────────┐
│ Corporate Network            │ │ VPC: 10.0.0.0/16       │
│ 192.168.0.0/16               │ │                         │
│ ┌──────────────────────────┐ │ │ ┌───────────────────┐   │
│ │ Corporate LAN            │ │ │ │ Private Subnet    │   │
│ │ Resources                │ │ │ │ 10.0.1.0/24       │   │
│ └──────┬───────────────────┘ │ │ │ ┌──────────┐      │   │
│        │                      │ │ │ │ Database │      │   │
│ ┌──────▼──────────────────────┤ │ │ └──────────┘      │   │
│ │ VPN Gateway / Router        │ │ └───────────────────┘   │
│ │ (Encryption/Decryption)     │ │          ▲              │
│ └──────┬──────────────────────┤ │          │              │
└────────┼──────────────────────┘ │ ┌────────▼─────────┐   │
         │ Encrypted Tunnel        │ │ VPN Endpoint     │   │
         │ (over Internet)          │ │ vpn-xxxxx        │   │
         │ IPSec/OpenVPN            │ │ (Encryption)     │   │
         │                          │ └──────────────────┘   │
         └──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┘
                                    │
                         ┌──────────▼──────────┐
                         │ AWS VPN Endpoint    │
                         │ Internet-based      │
                         │ Encrypted tunnel    │
                         └─────────────────────┘
```

#### Types of VPN Connections:

```
1. Site-to-Site VPN
   On-Premises → AWS VPC
   ├─ Connects whole networks
   ├─ Multiple VPNs for HA
   ├─ Static/Dynamic routing
   ├─ Bandwidth: Variable (~1.25 Gbps per connection)
   └─ Setup: VPN Gateway + Customer Gateway

2. AWS Client VPN
   Individual laptop → AWS VPC
   ├─ Secure remote access
   ├─ OpenVPN-based
   ├─ Per-user access control
   ├─ Scales to thousands of users
   └─ Pay per connection
```

#### VPN Setup Steps:

```bash
# Step 1: Create Virtual Private Gateway
aws ec2 create-vpn-gateway \
    --type ipsec.1 \
    --amazon-side-asn 64512

# Step 2: Attach to VPC
aws ec2 attach-vpn-gateway \
    --vpn-gateway-id vgw-xxxxx \
    --vpc-id vpc-xxxxx

# Step 3: Create Customer Gateway (on-premises end)
aws ec2 create-customer-gateway \
    --type ipsec.1 \
    --public-ip 203.0.113.100 \
    --bgp-asn 65000

# Step 4: Create VPN Connection
aws ec2 create-vpn-connection \
    --type ipsec.1 \
    --vpn-gateway-id vgw-xxxxx \
    --customer-gateway-id cgw-xxxxx

# Step 5: Enable route propagation
aws ec2 enable-vgw-route-propagation \
    --route-table-id rtb-xxxxx \
    --gateway-id vgw-xxxxx

# Step 6: Download VPN configuration
aws ec2 describe-vpn-connections \
    --vpn-connection-ids vpn-xxxxx \
    --query 'VpnConnections[0].CustomerGatewayConfiguration'
```

