### Load Balancer Health Checks:

```
Health Check Configuration:

Protocol: HTTP, HTTPS, TCP, UDP
Path: /health (for HTTP/HTTPS)
Port: 80, 443, or custom
Interval: 30 seconds (default)
Timeout: 5 seconds
Healthy Threshold: 2 consecutive checks
Unhealthy Threshold: 2 consecutive failures

Flow:
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Load Balancer Health Check:         │
│ GET http://10.0.1.10:80/health      │
└──────────┬──────────────────────────┘
           │
    ┌──────▼──────────┐
    │ EC2 Returns:    │
    │ 200 OK          │
    └──────┬──────────┘
           │
    ┌──────▼──────────┐
    │ Status: Healthy │
    │ Can receive     │
    │ traffic ✓       │
    └──────────────────┘

Failed Health Check:
EC2 doesn't respond / returns 500
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ Attempt 1: Timeout/Fail      │
│ Attempt 2: Timeout/Fail      │
│ (2 consecutive failures)     │
└──────────┬───────────────────┘
           │
    ┌──────▼──────────────┐
    │ Status: Unhealthy   │
    │ Removed from        │
    │ load balancing ✗    │
    └─────────────────────┘
```

### Sticky Sessions:

```
Without Sticky Sessions:
────────────────────────────────
User Request 1 → ALB → EC2-1 (Session created)
User Request 2 → ALB → EC2-2 (Session lost!)
User Request 3 → ALB → EC2-3 (Session lost!)

Problem: Session data not shared
Result: User keeps getting logged out

With Sticky Sessions (Duration-based):
────────────────────────────────────────
User Request 1 → ALB → EC2-1 (Session created)
                         (Cookie set: AWSALB=xxxxx)
User Request 2 → ALB → EC2-1 (Same server)
                        (Cookie matches)
User Request 3 → ALB → EC2-1 (Same server)
                        (Cookie still valid)

Duration expires or user clears cookies:
User Request 4 → ALB → EC2-2 (New server)

Configuration:
- Duration: 1 to 1 million seconds
- Default: 86400 seconds (1 day)
- Cookie name: AWSALB
```

